## API

The app reads and changes the data with the REST API of the FastAPI app
that appgen generates from the same definition. `src/shared/api/` has
the client: `http.ts` sends the requests, and `http-store.ts` maps the
JSON names of the API to the keys of the TypeScript types. The build
variable `VITE_API_URL` sets the URL of the API (default
`http://localhost:8000`):

```sh
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:8000 pnpm dev
```

The API must allow the origin of the app: set `CORS_ORIGINS` of the
FastAPI app, for example `["http://localhost:5173"]`. The list endpoints
filter only by equality, so the app loads all records of a list, and
searches, sorts, and pages them in the browser.
{% if definition.auth %}
The sign-in uses `POST /auth/sign-in` of the API, and each request sends
the token.
{% endif %}

{% endif %}
## Layout

The code follows [Feature-Sliced Design](https://feature-sliced.design).
Each layer can import only from the layers below it.

| Folder          | Layer                                                   |
| --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |
| `src/app/`      | The entry point, the providers, and the router.         |
| `src/pages/`    | One slice for each page of the definition.              |
| `src/widgets/`  | Large parts of a page, for example the app shell.       |
| `src/features/` | User actions, for example the forms.                    |
| `src/entities/` | The entity types and their data access.                 |
| `src/shared/`   | Code that does not know the domain: UI kit, lib, config. |

